            <section>
               <title value="Hospital course note"/>
               <code>
                  <coding>
                     <system value="http://loinc.org"/>
                     <code value="8648-8"/>
                     <display value="Hospital course note"/>
                  </coding>
               </code>
               <text>
                  <status value="generated"/>
                  <div xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml">Dear colleague, I am writing to inform you about the recent admission of your patient, a 76-year-old male, hospitalised on 23/02/2013 due to an acute exacerbation of his known chronic obstructive pulmonary disease (COPD). On admission, the patient presented with increased dyspnoea, productive cough, and reduced oxygen saturation. Clinical examination, chest X-ray, arterial blood gas analysis, and pulse oximetry confirmed the exacerbation. Blood tests were obtained to exclude secondary infection and other comorbidities. The patient was treated with supplemental oxygen therapy, inhaled bronchodilators via nebuliser, and a course of systemic corticosteroids. Vital signs were monitored closely throughout the stay. The patient responded well to treatment with significant symptomatic improvement. He was discharged on 24/02/2013 with optimised inhaler therapy and appropriate follow-up arranged. Patient education regarding inhaler technique and exacerbation management was provided prior to discharge.</div>
               </text>
            </section>
